.TH XSESSION 1 "2026-11-22" "Amiga UNIX add-on" "CDE"
.SH NAME
Xsession \- start a user's desktop session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/dt/bin/Xsession
.RB [ \-session
.IR name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR dtlogin (1)
runs
.B Xsession
as the user who logged in.
It sets up the session's environment and starts the session: CDE's
session manager,
.BR dtsession (1),
or, when the user chose it at the login screen, the user's own
.I \&.xsession
or
.I \&.xinitrc
(each only if executable); with none of these it starts a window manager
and a terminal.
.B \-session
names the session to start, as chosen at the login screen.
.PP
The environment comes from, in this order:
the user's
.IR \&.dtprofile ,
which the first login copies from
.I sys.dtprofile
.RI ( /etc/dt/config
before
.IR /usr/dt/config ),
sourced only when
.B ksh \-n
finds no error in it (otherwise the error goes to the start-up log);
the user's
.I \&.profile
or
.I \&.login
when
.I \&.dtprofile
sets
.BR DTSOURCEPROFILE=true ;
and every executable file in the
.I Xsession.d
directories
.RI ( /etc/dt/config/Xsession.d
before
.IR /usr/dt/config/Xsession.d ).
.SH FILES
.TP 30
.I $HOME/.dt/startlog
the session's start-up log
.TP
.I $HOME/.dt/errorlog
error messages of the session's programs
.TP
.I /etc/dt/config/Xsession.d
the administrator's start-up scripts
.SH NOTES
Do not edit
.IR /usr/dt/bin/Xsession ;
an update replaces it.
Local changes go in
.I /etc/dt/config/Xsession.d
or the user's
.IR \&.dtprofile .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dtlogin (1),
.BR dtsession (1)
